    "title": "Welcome to your NEXA workspace",
    "route": "(workspace)",
    "role": "all",
    "content": "## Welcome to your NEXA workspace\n\nNEXA is the shared table for a transaction—one place for documents, milestones, and messages instead of a dozen threads. You’ll only see what your role and participation allow; that’s by design, not a glitch.\n\n### How to get oriented\n\n1. Open **Help** (the **?** button) on any workspace screen to read guidance for where you are.\n2. Press **⌘K** (Mac) or **Ctrl+K** (Windows) anytime to search across every article—fast when you’re new.\n\n> **Remember:** Your coordinator still sets brokerage policy—software carries out what your office trains people to do.\n\n### Roles at a glance\n\n- **Transaction coordinators** — Pipeline, documents, checklists, signatures.\n- **Agents** — Client-facing updates scoped to their deals.\n- **Buyers & sellers** — Plain-language milestones and uploads—not internal chatter.\n- **Mortgage & title** — Condition-driven lanes that pair with your processor workflow.\n\nIf something feels missing, ask whether **your invite matches the work you’re doing**—scope beats clutter.\n"
