    "content": "## Managing Transaction Documents\n\nDocuments are the backbone of your file. Keep names predictable, categories honest, and signatures traceable—your title partner will thank you at wire.\n\n### Upload methods\n\nYou’ll usually see one or more paths—depending on how your brokerage configured NEXA:\n\n1. **Direct upload** — From the transaction **Documents** tab, choose **Upload**, pick category, attach the PDF or image.\n2. **Drag-and-drop** — When your browser supports it, drop files onto the upload zone—same category rules apply.\n3. **Email-in** — Some offices route a transaction-specific inbox (for example `deal+...@yourdomain`) into NEXA. Check with your admin—subject lines and routing rules matter.\n\n> **Note:** Email-in is powerful—also noisy. Train agents to include the transaction reference your policy requires.\n\n### Category organization\n\nCategories are how everyone finds things later—**contract**, **disclosure**, **title**, **mortgage**, **inspection**, **HOA**, **other**.\n\n1. Pick the closest truth—don’t stash disclosures under “other” because it’s faster today.\n2. If you must use **other**, add a bright filename (`Smith_COE_Addendum_v2.pdf`), not `scan001.pdf`.\n\n### Approving and rejecting\n\nWhen reviews are enabled:\n\n1. Open the tile—scan who uploaded it and when.\n2. Move status from **uploaded** toward **under review**, then **approved** when brokerage standards are met—reject with a clear note back to the sender.\n\n> **Warm professionalism:** Rejections land better with **what’s missing** and **who fixes it**—not just “noncompliant.”\n\n### Sending for signature\n\nFrom the manager (when DocuSign—or your e-sign—is wired):\n\n1. Choose the prepared PDF or packet.\n2. Launch your signing workflow—see **Sending Documents for Signature** for signer order and envelope hygiene.\n\n### Version history\n\nTreat uploads as progressive truth:\n\n1. Prefer **new uploads with clear version cues** (`Purchase_v3_final.pdf`) rather than overwriting silently where your system tracks revisions.\n2. When wire instructions change—**new PDF**, new acknowledgment—even if it feels bureaucratic.\n\n> **Gold standard:** One authoritative contract PDF per negotiation phase beats five ambiguous scans named “final_final.”\n"
