    "content": "## Sending Documents for Signature\n\nE-sign should feel inevitable—correct recipients, clean PDFs, signing order that matches how your brokerage negotiates (sign buyer before seller, or per attorney guidance).\n\n### Preparing a document\n\n1. Finalize the PDF on your side first—no half-filled placeholders unless everyone expects counters.\n2. Upload or select the packet within the transaction’s document manager.\n3. Confirm **page order**—especially exhibits and HOA amendments that riders reference.\n\n> **Gold rule:** Wire instructions never belong in the signing packet—send those through verified channels only.\n\n### Placing signature blocks\n\nIn DocuSign (or your configured provider):\n\n1. Drop fields where signers actually sign—initials on notice pages, full signatures on contract pages as law requires.\n2. Align dates **signer-local** where applicable—your provider handles locale formatting.\n\n### Selecting signers\n\n1. Map recipients to roles your brokerage expects—buyer, seller, broker associates where applicable.\n2. Set routing **order** deliberately—sequential when finance must see executed buyer docs before seller counters, parallel when independent.\n\n> **Remember:** Signers only see what you send in that envelope—double-check attachments before you launch.\n\n### What the signer sees\n\nThey’ll get an email with a secure link—inside:\n\n1. Page-by-page navigation (mobile-friendly on good templates).\n2. Required fields highlighted—less room for “I thought I signed everything.”\n\n### After signing\n\n1. Watch document status move toward **completed** in NEXA when webhooks are configured.\n2. Download the final composite PDF for your file copy—not just “it looked green in DocuSign.”\n\n### Voiding envelopes\n\nWhen something’s wrong mid-flight:\n\n1. Void from the provider with a **clear reason** recorded—your audit trail should read professional, not cryptic.\n2. Upload the corrected PDF and **send a fresh envelope**—avoid endless “replace page 7” ping-pong without version discipline.\n\n> **Important:** Voiding doesn’t unsay email—call conflict-prone parties when wires or identities were wrong.\n"
